    "text": "<p>The heat of reaction for</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#10230;</mo><mn>10</mn><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>)</mo></math> at constant volume is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1228</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kcal</mi></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>25</mn><mn>0</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The heat of reaction at constant pressure and same temperature is</p>"
